{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #111: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. If $G$ is a graph let $h_G(n)$ be defined such that any subgraph of $G$ on $n$ vertices can be made bipartite after deleting at most $h_G(n)$ edges.\n\nWhat is the behaviour of $h_G(n)$? Is it true that $h_G(n)/n\\to \\infty$ for every graph $G$ with chromatic number $\\aleph_1$? Current best: In \\cite{Er81} Erd\\H{o}s conjectured that this can be improved to $\\ll n^{1+\\epsilon}$ for every $\\epsilon>0$. Prize: no. Tags: chromatic number, graph theory, set theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_fe7a78d363e2adab125138ced540f77a679d6b463ce071ffc09b326c34d0beb3","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:111","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_3138df5d0acefa68","object_root":"sha256:e3aa5d892e25e0f9be75247022f89f4a095e680306cdff09b49a9a71c5471d04","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:111"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v